{"content":"I think the readability of this could be improved. ","codeSuggestion":"  // Do not update the dialog after an await if its source, draft, or save
  // operation has been replaced.
  const isCurrent = () => {
    const state = store.getState();
    const sourceSession = selectCalendarEventSourceSession(state, sessionKey);
    const draft = selectCalendarEventDraftState(state, sessionKey);
    const editSession = selectCalendarEventCreateEditSession(state, sessionKey);

    const hasCurrentSource = sourceSession?.requestId === source.requestId;
    const hasCurrentBaseline = draft?.baseline === baseline;
    const hasCurrentOperation = editSession?.operation?.requestId === requestId;

    return hasCurrentSource && hasCurrentBaseline && hasCurrentOperation;
  };","assessment":"The reviewer proposes named values for the three request checks. Apply that readability change in the edit-Save patch and preserve all three identity comparisons.","rationale":"isCurrent checks the source request, draft baseline object, and Save request. These checks protect different lifetimes. Named selector results and Boolean values make those roles easier to read.","recommendation":"change","validation":"Confirmed changeset 14134074, new-side lines 89–103, the native suggestion, and the author's reply. Inspected saveCalendarEventEdit, the operation reducers, and test_staleSuccessAndFailureCannotUpdateReplacement. That descendant integration test could not run from the selected checkout.","appliedSummary":"","changeSummary":"In Bug-2061218_4, refactor isCurrent in mail/components/calendar/content/calendar-event-edit-save.mjs to use named selector results and Boolean checks. Preserve the identity comparisons and all call sites.","state":"ready","changeAccepted":false,"changeReverted":false,"changesAmended":false}
